PURPOSE Define the paper's separate vehicle/package routes and shared interfaces.
INPUT selected case, space-time catalog, route and solver records
OUTPUT immutable identities, route coefficients, plans and search records
REFERENCES Point.cs; Arc.cs; ClassName/*.cs; DistinctItemComparer*.cs

RECORD Point
    fullId, pointType, layerType, x, y, serviceState
RECORD TimeWindow
    ownerId, pointType, lowerLimit, upperLimit
RECORD PointTW
    point, timeWindow, otherPoint, otherTimeWindow, submittedAt
RECORD SpaceTimeVertex
    ownerType, ownerId, pointIdentity, serviceState, time
RECORD SpaceTimeVertices
    tail: SpaceTimeVertex, head: SpaceTimeVertex
RECORD Arc
    recordId, ownerType, ownerId, family, arcType, tail, head
    duration, value, supportKey, serviceEvents, catalogId
RECORD VehicleRoute
    routeId, physicalVehicleId, orderedArcIds, cost, duration
    g[vehicle], serviceIncidence d[order], endpointIncidence B[stateTransition]
RECORD PackageRoute
    routeId, orderId, orderedArcIds, cost, coverage d[order]
    endpointIncidence b[stateTransition], fragments, transferEvents, isUnserved
    A complete package route has one master variable even when stored as r+/r-.
RECORD SplitRoute
    routeId, ownerId, kind, arcIds, serviceIncidence, endpointIncidence, cost
    paperRecord: VehicleRoute or PackageRoute
RECORD BranchDecision
    ownerKind, ownerId, catalogSignature, originalArcRecordId
    complete tail/head identities and times, value in {0,1}
    Alias ArcBranchDecision uses this record; source BB_info indices are decoded
        into these stable keys before search begins.
RECORD BranchNode
    id, parentId, depth, active, inheritedDecisions
    vehicleBranches, packageBranches, pool, status, branchSignature
    Node is an alias of BranchNode; nodeId is a reporting alias of id.
    bound: optional value with the scope/certificate that supplied it
RECORD Plan
    vehiclePaths, packagePaths, assignments, acceptedOrders, unservedOrders
    cost, modelIdentity, status, input
RECORD DynamicState
    previousPlan, decisionTime, implementationTime, completedPrefix
    inProgressArcs, residualSources, onboardOrders, acceptedUnfinishedOrders

INTERFACE RESULT RECORDS
    InputDataset{orders,vehicles,arrivals,selectedFiles,configuration}
    ArcResult{incumbent,objective,solverBound,status,arcMaps,assignments,plan,scope}
    MasterResult{status,solverStatus,objective,weights,duals,isIntegral,
                 fractionalCandidate,primalResidual,integralityResidual,
                 poolSignature,rowSignature,scope}
    columnWeights aliases weights; dualsByRowKey aliases duals.
    QuadraticResult{status,objective,weights,plan,bound,scope,
                    routePoolSignature,branchSignature}
    VehiclePricingResult{candidate,referenceRouteId,pricingObjective,solverStatus,
                         solverLowerBound,physicalCost,signatures}
    PackagePricingResult{candidate,pricingObjective,pricingStatus,pricingSolverBound,
                         physicalPackageCost,supportStatus,supportObjective,
                         supportingVehiclePaths}
    SplitResult{bestFeasiblePlan,status,pool,nodeHistories,initialSolutions,input,
                scope,globalLowerBound=unknown,relativeGap=unknown,unresolvedNodes}
    PricingBatch{results,candidates,diagnostics,status,counter,signatures}
    AdmissionResult{pool,inserted,duplicates,rejected,
                    hasNegativeDuplicate,hasContractFailure}
    RoutePool{vehicleRoutes,packageRoutes,g,dVehicle,dPackage,B,b,costs,
              A,A_transpose,B_transpose,routes,combinedRoutes,signature,
              catalogSignature,configuration}
    Unavailable objectives/solutions are none. A solver status alone is not a Plan.

PROCEDURE VertexEqual(left,right)
    compare owner type/id, full point identity, service state and time
    return equality

PROCEDURE SupportKey(arc)
    remove only the layer owner from both endpoint keys
    preserve complete service-point identities, state decorations and both times
    return the ordered endpoint pair under the catalog's compatibility mapping

PROCEDURE ArcEqual(left,right)
    compare catalogId and original recordId; verify all recorded fields agree
    return equality

PROCEDURE CloneNode(parent)
    copy mutable pools, decisions and status into independent containers
    share immutable catalog records; allocate a fresh node ID and solver model
    return child

PROCEDURE CheckViews(pool)
    REQUIRE exactly one cost and one validated path per route ID
    REQUIRE g[l,k] = 1 iff l belongs to physical vehicle k
    REQUIRE dPackage[q,r] = 1 iff q is a complete route choice for order r
    REQUIRE every r+/r- fragment points to exactly one complete package route
    REQUIRE forward/transposed A and B views agree, absent coefficients = 0
    REQUIRE service incidence dVehicle is distinct from physical ownership g
    REQUIRE coefficients and costs recompute from the same original arc records
    return valid

NOTES
    A package's penalized unserved route covers its route-choice row;
    isUnserved distinguishes that choice from physical service.
    Node copies share immutable catalogs and own their mutable state.
